- Main experiment: Table I public-code mainline, window 48; completed locally but numerical values were not reproduced.
- Selected core: Candidate A.
- Relationship to main: shared-base but outcome-independent. It retrains a dedicated few-shot generator and does not reuse main checkpoints.
- Main weakness does not logically predict the few-shot result; interpreting exact numerical agreement still depends on the same preprocessing/model audit.
- Post-main core gate: minimum viable Candidate A authorized by the user.

## Current stage

- Phase 3: FD001 minimum viable few-shot execution is running in `metaindux-fewshot-fd001.service`.
- Paper split: RUL > 30 normal; 10% fatigue included in generator training.
- Code boundary: RUL <= 30 fatigue because the paper leaves RUL=30 unstated.
- Generation seeds: 3, 13, 23, 33, 43; evaluator seeds identical.
- Next checkpoint: validate FD001 split counts and dry-run, then execute five generators and 25 fixed-split evaluations.

